  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "A square and an equilateral triangle have equal perimeters. The area of the triangle is \\(9\\sqrt3\\) square inches. Expressed in inches the diagonal of the square is:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac92\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(2\\sqrt5\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(4\\sqrt2\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac{9\\sqrt2}{2}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "none of these"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "d",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1962-p6.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "If \\(s\\) is the triangle’s side, then \\[ \\frac{\\sqrt3}{4}s^2=9\\sqrt3, \\] so \\(s=6.\\) Its perimeter is \\(18,\\) making the square’s side \\(\\frac{18}{4}=\\frac{9}{2}.\\) The square’s diagonal is therefore \\(\\frac{9\\sqrt2}{2}.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is D.",
      "hints": [
        "Use \\(\\frac{\\sqrt3}{4}s^2\\) for the triangle’s area",
        "Equate the two perimeters, then multiply the square’s side by \\(\\sqrt2\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
